  "scientific_takeaway": "The Severity-Gated Ensemble dynamically decouples the GBDT component during high-pollution episodes (yt > 180 ug/m3 for PM2.5), improving severe-tier PM2.5 bias from -21.97 to -17.58 ug/m3 and reducing severe MAE from 38.13 to 37.28 ug/m3, while preserving the overall benchmark MAE at 10.395 ug/m3. However, because the static blend is simpler and delivers identical overall benchmark MAE (10.40 ug/m3), the static blend remains the primary recommended baseline while the gated model serves as a validated severe-aware alternative."
